-## 11. `skill/`
+## 11. `skills/`
 
-[`skill/SKILL.md`](skill/SKILL.md) plus `skill/references/` (`lighthouse-mechanics.md`, `flow-metrics.md`, `coaching-patterns.md`) form an agent skill named `lighthouse`. It does two jobs: it tells an assistant how to reach Lighthouse (connected MCP tools first, then stdio, then HTTP, then the `lh` CLI) and how to call the tools correctly (id resolution, batching, forecast workflows), and it carries the flow-metrics coaching guidance used to interpret the results. It is plain Markdown with no build step. The release job zips the folder into the `lighthouse-skill.zip` release asset. Because it names CLI commands and MCP tools, keep it in step when either surface changes.
+Each folder under `skills/` is one agent skill, plain Markdown with no build step: a `SKILL.md` whose frontmatter `name` is the folder's name, optional `references/` the skill loads on a named condition, and `evals/` (cases and fixtures, never shipped).
+
+- **`lighthouse`** (`SKILL.md` plus `references/`) tells an assistant how to reach Lighthouse (connected MCP tools first, then stdio, then HTTP, then the `lh` CLI), names every MCP tool, `lh` subcommand and `--metrics` key with when to use it, and carries the flow-coaching stance used to interpret the results.
+- **`lighthouse-refinement`** and **`lighthouse-daily-flow-review`** name `lighthouse` as their companion instead of repeating it, and restate in one line each the rules they cannot run without (quote `summary`, use the instance's words, humans decide, never answer the usage-data question), because a skill can be installed alone.
+
+**Packing.** [`scripts/pack-skills.sh`](scripts/pack-skills.sh) zips each folder's contents (`SKILL.md` at the zip root, `evals/` left out) into `<name>-skill.zip`, so the general skill stays `lighthouse-skill.zip`. `verify` runs it and lists every zip; the release job attaches them all.
+
+**Drift test.** `skills/skills.drift.test.ts`, part of `pnpm test`, reads the tool names from `createMcpCoreRuntime(...).listTools()` and the groups, subcommands and metric keys from the help `runCliCommand` prints. It fails, naming each one, when the general skill leaves out a tool, subcommand or metric key, when any skill names one that does not exist, or when a skill's frontmatter `name` is not its folder's.
+
+**Evaluations.** `skills/<name>/evals/cases.json` holds prompts with the tool calls that must and must not happen and what the answer must and must not say; `evals/fixtures/*.json` are static Lighthouse answers served by [`scripts/eval-fixture.mjs`](scripts/eval-fixture.mjs), which logs every request. The maintainer runs them by hand before a release, as [`skills/README.md`](skills/README.md) describes; they are not part of CI.
